No project files found in the working directory, so I'll provide the implementation you can drop into your existing project.

You need two things: an `IExceptionHandler` implementation and the registration in `Program.cs`.

**1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourApp.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException   => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // Fall through to default handler (returns 500)

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title = title,
            Detail = title,           // Safe — never use exception.Message
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
// After builder creation, before Build()
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

// After Build(), before mapping endpoints
app.UseExceptionHandler();   // Catches exceptions, delegates to ApiExceptionHandler
app.UseStatusCodePages();    // Wraps bare status codes (e.g. 404) in Problem Details
```

**How it works:**

| Exception | Status | Problem Details `title` |
|---|---|---|
| `KeyNotFoundException` | 404 | Not Found |
| `ArgumentException` | 400 | Bad Request |
| `InvalidOperationException` | 409 | Conflict |
| Anything else | 500 | Generic (no leak) |

Unmatched exceptions return `false`, so the default `AddProblemDetails()` handler produces a safe 500 response with no stack trace or `exception.Message`.

No try-catch needed in endpoints — just `throw` normally:

```csharp
app.MapGet("/api/items/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    throw new KeyNotFoundException(); // → 404 Problem Details
});
```
